{"skill":{"slug":"content-stock","displayName":"content-stock"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1775550165039,"changelog":"- Rebranded the skill as \"content-stock\" with a new description and versioning.\n- Added SKILL.md and content_stock.js to support stock selection analysis based on news, keywords, or reports.\n- Removed the previous \"content\" skill documentation (skill.md).\n- New setup instructions: requires EASYALPHA_API_KEY and usage examples provided.\n- Supports two analysis depths: \"fast\" and \"deep\".","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"content_stock.js","size":1458,"sha256":"1446cca67e8f0bce454a789e7c09fa207ac65564db34b6856d6464e749736d35","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":921,"sha256":"27b5db11a41a22527f1ac10a580978d49af1382be2477bd6d25b4d043384695d","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1595,"sha256":"e0fe84d4bbd7235a95fdcf766d4b1a101d242842f1629d1a0ceeaf82670f3a2c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789535881188,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"58bb54bb2fea32cccb5ea2426eda6b5f77a8442d53bc444d356f85134147616f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/58bb54bb2fea32cccb5ea2426eda6b5f77a8442d53bc444d356f85134147616f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090331507},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":66,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789535881188},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This stock-analysis skill is purpose-aligned, but it sends the API key and user queries over unencrypted HTTP, which puts credentials and potentially sensitive research at risk.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of an API key and network call is proportionate to an external analysis service, but content_stock.js posts both the bearer token and user query to a plaintext http:// endpoint.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The required artifact is mostly plain Markdown with OpenClaw metadata for one environment variable and node, but it contains two trailing NUL bytes that make the file malformed; inspection found no hidden content after them.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documentation tells users to set EASYALPHA_API_KEY and call get_content_stock, but it does not clearly disclose that queries are transmitted to a remote service or identify a real trusted endpoint.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, local file indexing, privilege escalation, tool hijacking, background worker, or destructive local behavior was found in the inspected artifacts.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill coherently implements a content-stock analysis helper that sends a query and analysis depth to an external EasyAlpha-style API and streams the response.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Only use this skill if the endpoint is changed to HTTPS with a trusted hostname, the API key is scoped and rotatable, and users understand that their stock-analysis queries are sent to an external service. Remove the malformed trailing NUL bytes from SKILL.md before publishing.","findings":"[AE3] unexpected: Confirmed two trailing NUL bytes in SKILL.md. They are not purpose-aligned and should be removed, but they did not hide additional instructions or code in this artifact.\n[LP3] expected: The skill's need for an API key and network access is expected for an external analysis integration, though the artifact does not provide tight permission or destination scoping.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending user stock-analysis queries to an external service is consistent with the skill purpose, but the documentation under-discloses that data flow.\n[SDI-2] expected: Reading EASYALPHA_API_KEY from the environment is declared in the metadata and usage instructions and is coherent for API authentication.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Confirmed content_stock.js uses a plaintext http:// endpoint while sending Authorization: Bearer credentials and the user query; this is the main Review concern.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese documentation and comments appear aligned with a Chinese-language stock-selection workflow and are not, by themselves, a security concern.\n[T09] unexpected: Static scan's plaintext credential/query transmission finding is supported by the code at content_stock.js lines 15-29.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789535881188}}}}}